  "mathematicalFinding": "D, E, F are the side midpoints, so AE, BF and CD are the medians and G is their intersection. The six small triangles have equal area. BEGD is exactly the union of BDG and BEG, hence 2 of the 6 equal parts: 90*(2/6)=30 square centimetres, matching choice 1. The source solution and illustrated two-part region agree.",
  "definitionFinding": "The proposed template describes this pure median equal-area partition. It is not coordinate averaging, vertex recovery or a distance-square relation, and it does not replace the primary NEW_TPL debt with a cross-concept tag. The existing parent explicitly covers median properties. The proposal is narrowed to one triangle with its three medians and unions of the resulting six cells; unreviewed repeated-centroid constructions are excluded.",
